  "claim_boundary": "This proof starts from the fixed empty gameplay-frame-1 state and executes 228 linked Reimu-A rank-1 transitions using only replay input masks. It composes the prior enclosing Player/bullet/Enemy kernel with persistent collided-bullet motion and ANM timers, 253 AABB damage calls, five collision transitions in slots 2/3/4/0/1, all five first-wave deaths, target selection, and score 1950. Every active Player bullet and retained Enemy raw-bit projection is publicly committed. Retail Wine and the independently built Linux reference match over 260 frames. This is finite differential and static-mapping evidence, not a universal retail-binary equivalence proof. The kernel stops at frame 229 because death-spawned item state is omitted and first feeds retained score/power at frame 249. RNG/effect and Sub0 shooting noninterference, direct collision-ANM decoding, x87 fsincos refinement, translation validation, and later gameplay subsystems remain explicit obligations."
